Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>

meson-amvdec: AV1 on T7 - program the parser front-end from the host

The S4 and SC2 AV1 microcode programs the stream and parser front-end
(HEVC_SHIFT_STARTCODE/EMULATECODE, CABAC_CONTROL, PARSER_CORE_CONTROL,
PARSER_IF_CONTROL, PARSER_INT_CONTROL, SHIFT_STATUS) itself as soon as
data arrives, and stops on the sequence header (status 0xf2). The T7
microcode leaves all of them at their reset values, never starts parsing
and only answers AOM_NAL_DECODE_DONE (0x25), so no AV1 stream can be
decoded.

The vendor driver writes these registers from the host. Do the same on
SoCs flagged with the new av1_host_parser platform capability, set for T7.
All of the registers are needed: each subset tried on its own leaves the
microcode on 0x25.

